;	000000000300090670	;	"	<p><strong>Dihydroberberine SR 150mg</strong> is ideal for men and women who want an effective nutritional therapy for glucose balance, lipid metabolism and cardiovascular health that is both well-tolerated and convenient. Formulated to complement doctor-recommended diet and lifestyle changes.*</p> <p><strong>Dihydroberberine SR 150mg</strong> is a sustained-release dietary supplement featuring GlucoVantage<sup>®</sup> dihydroberberine, a highly bioavailable form of berberine. Once absorbed by the intestine, dihydroberberine rapidly converts to berberine in blood.<sup>1</sup> Berberine has been widely studied in pre-clinical and clinical studies. It’s ability to positively affect glucose balance, lipid metabolism and blood vessel health is attributed to multiple actions. For example:</p> <ul style=""list-style-type: disc;""> <li><strong>Glucose Balance</strong>. Results from pre-clinical studies indicate berberine activates a key biochemical pathway – the AMPactivated protein kinase (AMPK) pathway – that plays a role in glucose uptake by tissues.<sup>2</sup></li> <li><strong>Lipid Metabolism</strong>. Results from pre-clinical studies indicate berberine promotes healthy cholesterol metabolism by a variety of actions. First, it upregulates LDL-receptors on liver cells that shuttle cholesterol out of the blood and into cells. Berberine inhibits intestinal cholesterol absorption and increases excretion as well as provides antioxidant defense. By activating AMPK, it also increases fatty acid oxidation (burning) and decreases fatty acid synthesis.<sup>3</sup></li> <li><strong>Blood Vessel Function</strong>. Results from pre-clinical studies indicate berberine promotes healthy endothelial function, an action attributed in part to its ability to reduce oxidative stress.<sup>4</sup></li> </ul> <p>As a highly bioavailable form of berberine, Dihydroberberine SR may help maintain healthy blood glucose and lipid levels in the normal range while supporting vascular health.*</p>"
;	000000000300084660	;	"	<p>EP Dihydroberberine with glucovantage, utilizing our proprietary sustained release vegetable wax matrix technology for maximum bioavailability. Backed with clinical reviews the positively charged berberine is converted in the gut to it's metabolite, dihydroberberine, a neutral charge, a highly bioavailable form to penetrate cells. Pre-clinical research shows berberine activates numerous metabolic and cardiovascular pathways and thereby may help promote glucose balance, healthy cholesterol and lipid metabolism and vascular health.*  </p>"
;	000000000300090784	;	"	<ul style=""list-style-type: disc;""> <li>Supportive blend of natural indole compounds*</li> <li>May help support healthy estrogen metabolism*</li> <li>May help support cellular health*</li> <li>May help support liver health*</li> </ul> <p>DIM + I3C by Seeking Health contains 400 mg of dietary indoles, naturally occurring components of cruciferous vegetables that may help support the body's healthy estrogen metabolism processes. DIM (diindolylmethane) is a metabolic byproduct of I3C (indole-3- carbinol), a compound found in broccoli, cabbage and other vegetables in the Brassicacae family. These well-known indoles are combined with other related compounds to provide a broad spectrum of support for processing estrogen metabolites, such as 16-alpha hydroxyestrone. Indole compounds may help support normal hormone metabolism and estrogen processing in favor of a healthy ratio of estrogen metabolites.*</p>"
;	000000000300102786	;	"	<p class=""p1"">Diindolylmethane, also known as DIM, is a gastric metabolite of indole compounds found in cruciferous vegetables. DIM promotes healthy estrogen metabolism by helping to breakdown estrogens in the body, shifting the estrogen balance towards the formation of beneficial metabolites and away from harmful ones. This unique formula contains therapeutic dosages of Diindolylmethane (DIM) and its cofactors—a full array of nutrients that work synergistically to support normal estrogen ratios.*<span class=""Apple-converted-space""> </span></p>"
;	000000000300000571	;	"	<p><strong>DIMension 3<sup>®</sup></strong> represents a three-dimensional approach to supporting healthy estrogen metabolism. Research suggests that diindolylmethane (DIM), curcumin (from turmeric extract), and the patented black pepper extract BioPerine<sup>®</sup> support balanced estrogen metabolism.*</p>"
