;	000000000300092177	;	"	<p>PREMIER RESEARCH LABS MELATONIN-ND<sup>™</sup> A nutritional industry first, featuring melatonin in a convenient liquid form that has been cultured with beneficial probiotic organisms for active bio-availability. Melatonin-ND<sup>™</sup> is not animal-derived so it is suitable for everyone, including vegetarians and vegans. This premier quality formula is fermented using a unique probiotic culture which allows rapid delivery and superior bioenergetic dynamics. Many people say they can feel the effect of this product the very first time they take it.</p>"
;	000000000300000973	;	"	<p><strong>MemorAll<sup>™</sup></strong> is a unique combination of nutrients and botanicals that supports cognitive function and a healthy memory. It features select B vitamins, including Quatrefolic<sup>®</sup>, a patented form of 5-MTHF; the herbs <em>Gingko biloba</em> and <em>Bacopa monnieri</em>; nutrients that provide antioxidant activity; and brain-specific nutrients such as acetyl-L-carnitine and sunflower-derived phosphatidylserine. This comprehensive formula addresses the multiple pathways involved in neurological health by supporting oxidant and cytokine balance, methylation, mitochondrial function, and endocrine balance.*</p>"
;	000000000300084742	;	"	<p>Memory is a combination of two herbs traditionally used in Ayurveda to support healthy nervous system function and cognition. This formula contains Gotu Kola, a nootropic herb used for centuries as a tonic for overall brain and nervous system support and has long been prized by students and yogis for its calming support of the nervous system. Memory also contains the nootropic Bacopa, which the ancient Vedics classified as a “Medya Rasayana,” or “rejuvenator of the intellect,” The formula also adds Shankpushpi, which Ayurveda suggests for recovery from intensive studying, computer work, and memorization. Gluten Free, Vegan, USDA Certified Organic, Non GMO Project Verified</p>"
;	000000000300088150	;	"	<p>In healthy brains, proteins that inhibit healthy cognition and memory are created, but they are regularly cleared through normal processes.<sup>1</sup> This clearing process declines over time as part of normal aging. When that happens, these proteins begin to accumulate, affecting memory and cognitive function.<sup>2</sup></p> <p>Colostrinin is a milk peptide that helps inhibit molecular mechanisms that produce unwanted brain proteins, while also maintaining levels of the enzymes that help break them down.<sup>3</sup></p> <p>Lithium is a naturally-occurring mineral that preclinical studies show helps support the breakdown of those accumulated brain proteins and promotes the brain’s normal process for clearing cellular debris .<sup>12</sup></p> <p> </p> <p><strong>Reference:</strong><br />1. <em>Neurotox Res.</em> 2018;34(3):733-748.<br />2. <em>Pathol Int</em>. 2017;67(4):185-193.<br />3. <em>J Nutr Health Aging</em>. 2009;13(3):235-41.<br />4. <em>Arch Immunol Ther Exp (Warsz)</em>. 1999;47(6):377-85.<br />5. <em>Med Sci Monit</em>. 2002;8(10):PI93-6.<br />6. <em>J Alzheimers Dis</em>. 2004;6(1):17-26.<br />7. <em>Neurodegenerative Dis</em>. 2007;4(suppl 1):264.<br />8. <em>Neuropsychopharmacology</em>. 2018;43(5):1174-1179.<br />9. <em>Journal of American Physicians and Surgeons</em>. 2015;20(4)<br />10. <em>Curr Alzheimer Res</em>. 2016;13(8):862-72.<br />11. <em>Neuropsychiatr Dis Treat</em>. 2013;9:493-500.<br />12. <em>ACS Chem Neurosci</em>. 2014;5(6):434-42.<br />13. <em>Aust N Z J Psychiatry</em>. 2014;48(9):809-18.</p>"
;	000000000300101123	;	"	<p>Menopause 731™ uses a clinically studied extract of Siberian rhubarb (R. rhaponticum) root to address 11 common menopausal discomforts: hot flashes, night sweats, irritability, mood swings, sleep disturbances, exhaustion, joint and muscle discomfort, vaginal dryness, urinary health and sexual function.</p>"
